      },
      "review": "All reference capability families mapped to fixed and native widths. Independent edge/random arithmetic, every eight-bit reversal, signed rotation boundaries, zero/overflow errors and guarded raw kernels are tested. Usize paths also cross-compile for 32-bit Wasm; ARM and big-endian PowerPC checks compile kernels without claiming execution on those targets. All ten word-operation tests also pass with the updated self-built compiler, including proof-bearing division and signed/unsigned machine ordering boundaries. Functional coverage does not assert matching allocation costs or division throughput."
